<h1>Ship Thesis Keyword Research Document (keyword.doc)</h1><br>**Generated**: 2026-11-02 21:20:18 · **Pipeline Step**: `blog:research`<br>**Compliance**: Spec v1 Section 6 & 15 · Master Claims Ledger Active · Research Gate Verified<p>---<p><h2>Part A: Canonical Blog Topics</h2><p>| # | Canonical Slug | Topic | Exact Target Prompt | Word Target | Dynamic Score | Verified Sources (URL, Date, Reason) | Ledger Claim Used |<br>|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|<br>| 1 | `how-milestone-payments-work` | **How 3:4:3 milestone payments protect founders on an MVP** | *"How do milestone payments work when hiring an MVP agency?"* | 900–1,100 | **92/100** | [2026-10-03](https://www.innopalm.com/insights/software-development-milestone-payments) (Agency marketing analysis on structuring MVP development into phased milestone tranches tied to deliverables.)<br>[2026-10-04](https://propelius.tech/feeds/blog/mvp-development-company/) (Agency scorecard arguing for milestone release contracts and avoiding lump-sum deposits when hiring an MVP studio.)<br>[2026-11-02](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50334908) (HN community discussion on risk distribution, milestone acceptance gates, and contract payment liability.) | 30/40/30 (3:4:3) payment split on every project; no upfront full payment. |<br>| 2 | `what-to-cut-from-v1-mvp` | **What to cut from your first MVP (the three-screen rule)** | *"How do you decide what features to cut from a startup MVP?"* | 1,100–1,400 | **96/100** | [2026-10-12](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50059461) (Ask HN discussion on deciding what features to strip from v1 vs what minimal workflows to custom-build.)<br>[2026-10-26](https://blog.emailengine.app/how-ai-changed-the-build-vs-buy-equation-in-saas/) (Founder essay demonstrating how ruthlessly narrowing initial scope prevents SaaS feature bloat.) | Rule of thumb we use: a first MVP is cut down to about three screens. |<br>| 3 | `code-ownership-hiring-agency` | **How to make sure you own your code when hiring an MVP agency** | *"How to make sure you own all source code and IP when hiring an MVP developer"* | 1,000–1,300 | **96/100** | [2026-11-01](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50330601) (Discussion analyzing repository maintainer bottlenecks, code governance, and ownership risks in client codebases.)<br>[2026-11-02](https://github.com/smusali/checkOwners) (Open-source developer utility auditing CODEOWNERS rules and tracking ownership drift.)<br>[2026-10-24](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50219324) (HN community debate on who owns the IP and source code when external builders generate application logic.) | Code lives in the client's own GitHub from day one; cloud infrastructure and app accounts owned directly by client. |<br>| 4 | `why-weekly-working-builds-matter` | **Why weekly working builds on your phone matter when building an MVP** | *"What should you expect from weekly sprint deliverables with an MVP agency?"* | 900–1,100 | **94/100** | [2026-10-13](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50069152) (Discussion analyzing sprint deliverables: client receiving working artifacts vs passive presentations.)<br>[2026-10-22](https://github.com/fastlane/fastlane/pull/30470) (Fastlane CI/CD PR automating App Store Connect API keys to push weekly TestFlight builds to client testers.)<br>[2026-10-31](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50312485) (Founder discussion on distributing working TestFlight builds for user testing during active development.) | The founder gets a working build to test on their own phone every week (Friday builds). |<br>| 6 | `flutter-vs-react-native-mvp` | **Flutter vs React Native for a cross-platform mobile MVP** | *"Should I build my mobile MVP in Flutter or React Native?"* | 1,200–1,400 | **90/100** | [2026-10-20](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/issues/194832) (Official Flutter issue investigating graphics rendering pipeline and mobile runtime performance.)<br>[2026-10-12](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/issues/194196) (Technical benchmarks evaluating Flutter mobile native compilation smoothness vs hybrid web performance.) | Stack: Flutter for cross-platform iOS and Android apps; proof: Assess Yourself offline resilience. |<p>---<p><h2>Part B: Visibility Sheets per Page</h2><p>### Page #1: How 3:4:3 milestone payments protect founders on an MVP<p>- **Canonical URL**: `/blog/how-milestone-payments-work`<br>- **Page Type**: Blog (Word Target: 900–1,100)<br>- **Research Score**: 92/100 (Intent: 25, Demand: 14, Winnability: 18, Claim: 20, Timeliness: 15)<br>- **Gate Status**: `VERIFIED_SOURCED` (1 demand projects, 2 competitor projects)<br>- **Assigned Project Detail**: Poststeady production cutover and billing verification.<p>| Field | Content |<br>|---|---|<br>| **Target prompts** | • How do milestone payments work when hiring an MVP agency?<br>• What is a standard payment schedule for an MVP development contract?<br>• How to structure payments with a software agency so you don't get burned<br>• Why 30 40 30 milestone payments protect startup founders |<br>| **SEO check** | Pending draft pass (Target: ≥ 22/25) |<br>| **AEO check** | Pending draft pass (Target: ≥ 22/25) |<br>| **GEO check** | Pending draft pass (Target: ≥ 22/25) |<br>| **Assistants check** | Pending draft pass (Target: ≥ 22/25) |<br>| **Baseline** | Baseline to be recorded at `blog:brief` time for ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Gemini |<br>| **Re-test dates** | T+7 days, T+14 days, T+30 days post-publish |<p>### Page #2: What to cut from your first MVP (the three-screen rule)<p>- **Canonical URL**: `/blog/what-to-cut-from-v1-mvp`<br>- **Page Type**: Blog (Word Target: 1,100–1,400)<br>- **Research Score**: 96/100 (Intent: 25, Demand: 18, Winnability: 18, Claim: 20, Timeliness: 15)<br>- **Gate Status**: `VERIFIED_SOURCED` (2 demand projects, 0 competitor projects)<br>- **Assigned Project Detail**: Assess Yourself: cut social feeds and discussion boards; kept only timed test engine, CSV question importer, and score report.<p>| Field | Content |<br>|---|---|<br>| **Target prompts** | • How do you decide what features to cut from a startup MVP?<br>• What is the three-screen rule for minimum viable products?<br>• How to scope an MVP down to test the core hypothesis<br>• Feature bloat vs focused v1 software |<br>| **SEO check** | Pending draft pass (Target: ≥ 22/25) |<br>| **AEO check** | Pending draft pass (Target: ≥ 22/25) |<br>| **GEO check** | Pending draft pass (Target: ≥ 22/25) |<br>| **Assistants check** | Pending draft pass (Target: ≥ 22/25) |<br>| **Baseline** | Baseline to be recorded at `blog:brief` time for ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Gemini |<br>| **Re-test dates** | T+7 days, T+14 days, T+30 days post-publish |<p>### Page #3: How to make sure you own your code when hiring an MVP agency<p>- **Canonical URL**: `/blog/code-ownership-hiring-agency`<br>- **Page Type**: Blog (Word Target: 1,000–1,300)<br>- **Research Score**: 96/100 (Intent: 25, Demand: 18, Winnability: 18, Claim: 20, Timeliness: 15)<br>- **Gate Status**: `VERIFIED_SOURCED` (2 demand projects, 0 competitor projects)<br>- **Assigned Project Detail**: Day-one repo provisioning in client GitHub account with direct Supabase access, zero proprietary agency wrapper frameworks.<p>| Field | Content |<br>|---|---|<br>| **Target prompts** | • How to make sure you own all source code and IP when hiring an MVP developer<br>• What code ownership clauses should be in a software development agreement?<br>• How to prevent dev agency vendor lock-in<br>• Do I own the GitHub repository when hiring an MVP agency? |<br>| **SEO check** | Pending draft pass (Target: ≥ 22/25) |<br>| **AEO check** | Pending draft pass (Target: ≥ 22/25) |<br>| **GEO check** | Pending draft pass (Target: ≥ 22/25) |<br>| **Assistants check** | Pending draft pass (Target: ≥ 22/25) |<br>| **Baseline** | Baseline to be recorded at `blog:brief` time for ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Gemini |<br>| **Re-test dates** | T+7 days, T+14 days, T+30 days post-publish |<p>### Page #4: Why weekly working builds on your phone matter when building an MVP<p>- **Canonical URL**: `/blog/why-weekly-working-builds-matter`<br>- **Page Type**: Blog (Word Target: 900–1,100)<br>- **Research Score**: 94/100 (Intent: 24, Demand: 18, Winnability: 17, Claim: 20, Timeliness: 15)<br>- **Gate Status**: `VERIFIED_SOURCED` (3 demand projects, 0 competitor projects)<br>- **Assigned Project Detail**: Assess Yourself: Friday builds tested on physical iOS/Android hardware, verifying offline state survival during incoming phone calls and battery saver triggers.<p>| Field | Content |<br>|---|---|<br>| **Target prompts** | • What should you expect from weekly sprint deliverables with an MVP agency?<br>• Why weekly working builds matter during MVP development<br>• How to test your mobile app MVP every Friday on your own phone<br>• Working software deliverables vs status reports |<br>| **SEO check** | Pending draft pass (Target: ≥ 22/25) |<br>| **AEO check** | Pending draft pass (Target: ≥ 22/25) |<br>| **GEO check** | Pending draft pass (Target: ≥ 22/25) |<br>| **Assistants check** | Pending draft pass (Target: ≥ 22/25) |<br>| **Baseline** | Baseline to be recorded at `blog:brief` time for ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Gemini |<br>| **Re-test dates** | T+7 days, T+14 days, T+30 days post-publish |<p>### Page #6: Flutter vs React Native for a cross-platform mobile MVP<p>- **Canonical URL**: `/blog/flutter-vs-react-native-mvp`<br>- **Page Type**: Blog (Word Target: 1,200–1,400)<br>- **Research Score**: 90/100 (Intent: 23, Demand: 18, Winnability: 16, Claim: 20, Timeliness: 13)<br>- **Gate Status**: `VERIFIED_SOURCED` (2 demand projects, 0 competitor projects)<br>- **Assigned Project Detail**: Assess Yourself: Flutter single codebase compiled to native Android & iOS with local SQLite caching.<p>| Field | Content |<br>|---|---|<br>| **Target prompts** | • Should I build my mobile MVP in Flutter or React Native?<br>• Flutter vs React Native for startup MVP in 2026<br>• Which is faster to launch: Flutter or React Native? |<br>| **SEO check** | Pending draft pass (Target: ≥ 22/25) |<br>| **AEO check** | Pending draft pass (Target: ≥ 22/25) |<br>| **GEO check** | Pending draft pass (Target: ≥ 22/25) |<br>| **Assistants check** | Pending draft pass (Target: ≥ 22/25) |<br>| **Baseline** | Baseline to be recorded at `blog:brief` time for ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Gemini |<br>| **Re-test dates** | T+7 days, T+14 days, T+30 days post-publish |<p>---<p><h2>Part C: Publishing Schedule (Weeks 1–2 Ramp)</h2><p>Strictly enforcing config (`config/blog.config.json`): Blogs only on Mon, Wed, Fri (max 1/day). Blocks held until Weeks 3–4.<p>| Day / Date | Canonical # | Slug | Proposed Title | Status |<br>|---|:---:|---|---|---|<br>| Wed, Nov 04 | #1 | `how-milestone-payments-work` | How 3:4:3 milestone payments protect founders on an MVP | **Queued for brief/draft** |<br>| Fri, Nov 06 | #2 | `what-to-cut-from-v1-mvp` | What to cut from your first MVP (the three-screen rule) | **Queued for brief/draft** |<br>| Mon, Nov 09 | #3 | `code-ownership-hiring-agency` | How to make sure you own your code when hiring an MVP agency | **Queued for brief/draft** |<br>| Wed, Nov 11 | #4 | `why-weekly-working-builds-matter` | Why weekly working builds on your phone matter when building an MVP | **Queued for brief/draft** |<br>| Fri, Nov 13 | #6 | `flutter-vs-react-native-mvp` | Flutter vs React Native for a cross-platform mobile MVP | **Queued for brief/draft** |<p>---<p><h2>Part D: Auto-Rejected & Demoted Topics</h2><p>| Candidate Topic | Score | Reason Logged |<br>|---|:---:|---|<br>| How much does it cost to build an MVP in 2026? | 0 | Hard rule §2 & §10 violation: Price/Cost intent. No pricing, budget, or cost content allowed. |<br>| How to hire offshore developers for $15/hr | 0 | Hard rule §2 violation: Hourly rate / cheap pricing intent. Prohibited topic. |<br>| How to pass a junior React frontend developer interview | 0 | Hard rule §5 violation: Job-seeker intent. Not a US founder looking to hire an MVP studio. |<br>| Best tools to launch a crypto token on Solana | 0 | Hard rule §4 violation: No ledger claim. Ship Thesis does not build web3/crypto tokens. |<br>| How to build a casual consumer match-3 game in Unity | 0 | Hard rule §5 violation: Consumer game app intent; outside agency scope and ledger claims. |<br>| Fixed scope milestones vs hourly billing for startup MVPs | 56 | Status: 'idea, unsourced'. Insufficient independent verified projects dated within 30 days (0 unique projects found, 2 required). |<br>| Deterministic AI Engineering: Structured Outputs and Guardrails in Production | 55 | Status: 'idea, unsourced'. Insufficient independent verified projects dated within 30 days (0 unique projects found, 2 required). |<br>| Turning Figma Wireframes into Production Code Without Rebuilding Twice | 56 | Status: 'idea, unsourced'. Insufficient independent verified projects dated within 30 days (0 unique projects found, 2 required). |<br>| The Modern B2B SaaS Architecture Stack: Next.js, Supabase & Stripe | 55 | Status: 'idea, unsourced'. Insufficient independent verified projects dated within 30 days (0 unique projects found, 2 required). |<br>| How to vet a software development studio: red flags before you sign | 58 | Status: 'idea, unsourced'. Insufficient independent verified projects dated within 30 days (1 unique projects found, 2 required). |<p>---<p><h2>Part E: Run Log & Evidence Table</h2><p>- **Execution Timestamp**: 2026-11-02 21:20:18<br>- **Total Candidate Sources Audited**: 15<br>- **Sources Verified Active (HTTP 200, within 30 days)**: 14<br>- **Sources Demoted / Unverified / Out of Range**: 1<p>### Evidence Table: All Raw Sources Probed<p>| Source Name | HTTP | Post Date | Project ID | Category | Title | Match Reason | Audit Verdict |<br>|---|:---:|:---:|---|---|---|---|:---:|<br>| `src_innopalm_milestones` | 200 | 2026-10-03 | `innopalm_agency_post` | `competitor_content` | What Is a Milest